---
/**
 * foodcraft / WhyBO — "WHY-US" (Sipsip Tea Bar / BO).
 *
 * ROLE. The argument block, and the only section in this template that argues
 * rather than describes, lists or shows. A CENTRED head — a lilac pill eyebrow
 * over one Baloo 2 headline — and beneath it a STACK of full-width white
 * cards, each drawn as a horizontal pair: a 76px pastel MEDALLION carrying an
 * ordinal numeral, then the reason's title and the owner's paragraph beside it.
 * No photo, no price, no button, no link. The cards float on the page's own
 * blush ground; nothing here is banded and nothing is ruled.
 *
 * THE DESIGN IS THE SPECIFICATION. Every metric below is lifted verbatim from
 * "Sipsip Tea Bar Landing.dc.html", data-component="WHY-US". No literal hex
 * appears in this file (R1) — the colours are the wrapper tokens whose VALUES
 * are the design's hexes:
 *   eyebrow ground #EEE2F5 -> --lilac       eyebrow ink  #5C3580 -> --accent-deep
 *   headline       #241A22 -> --ink         emphasis     #7B4FA8 -> --accent
 *   card ground    #FFFFFF -> --card        title        #241A22 -> --ink
 *   paragraph      #5D5158 -> --ink-soft
 *   medallion 1    #EEE2F5 / #5C3580 -> --lilac  / --accent-deep
 *   medallion 2    #F7DCE7 / #5C2A45 -> --pink-2 / --plum
 *   medallion 3    #E3EFDC / #3C5C2A -> --sage   / --on-sage
 * EVERY colour this section draws has a token. Unlike TrustBO — whose fourth
 * badge is a warm amber the wrapper does not name — the WHY-US trio is exactly
 * the three declared ground/on-colour pairs, so nothing here is a substitution.
 *
 *   section   padding:80px 28px 0            head    text-align:center; mb:34px
 *   eyebrow   11px/700, .14em, uppercase, pill, padding:8px 16px
 *   h2        clamp(30px,4vw,52px); line-height:1.08; margin:.24em 0 0
 *   card      #FFF; border-radius:28px; padding:30px 34px; margin-bottom:14px
 *   card grid minmax(0,88px) minmax(0,1fr); gap:26px; align-items:center
 *   medallion 76x76; border-radius:50%; Baloo 2 700 32px
 *   title     Baloo 2 600 26px; margin:0 0 7px
 *   body      15.5px / 1.78; margin:0; max-width:64ch
 *
 * EDITABLE HOOKS. Every path below is declared in
 * components/editor/genericContentSchema.ts under the "Why us" group (id:
 * 'why'), so the sidebar owns a real input for each — a data-field on any other
 * path is a dead hook that focuses nothing:
 *   why.tag                — the eyebrow. Rides the wrapper's .kick primitive
 *                            (face, weight, 11px, uppercase) so the wrapper's
 *                            520 pass still re-sizes it; only the design's
 *                            .14em tracking, its --accent-deep ink and its
 *                            lilac pill are stated locally, and each of those
 *                            needs the .sip-why-head qualifier to land at all
 *                            (see SPECIFICITY below). font-size is
 *                            DELIBERATELY not restated: the QUALIFIED selector
 *                            does out-specify the wrapper's :where(.kick), so
 *                            restating it here would silently cancel that pass.
 *   why.headline           — the h2, rendered with set:html so an owner's own
 *                            <em> picks up PageBO's emphasis, which in this
 *                            template is a COLOUR CHANGE to --accent and not an
 *                            italic (Baloo 2 has no italic; asking for one
 *                            synthesises an oblique that fights its rounded
 *                            terminals). That rule is GLOBAL in the wrapper on
 *                            purpose: scoped styles cannot reach elements
 *                            created by set:html (R3), so any rule this file
 *                            ever needs for that <em> must be written
 *                            :global(). None is needed today — the wrapper
 *                            already de-italicises it and recolours it.
 *   why.items.${i}.title   — the reason (h3). Escaped, not set:html.
 *   why.items.${i}.body    — the reason's paragraph. Escaped. CANONICAL key:
 *                            the value can arrive as .description through
 *                            lib/astro-builder.ts's normalizeBlock alias map
 *                            (line ~897 spells { description: 'body' }), and as
 *                            .desc from older payloads, so the READ tolerates
 *                            all three while the data-field always spells the
 *                            key the schema declares — otherwise the sidebar
 *                            never receives the edit.
 *
 * R2 — NOTHING VISIBLE IS SUPPLIED BY THIS FILE. Not one word. The design's
 * demo copy ("Why us", "What makes it taste right.", "You choose the sugar")
 * is the DESIGNER filling in their own template; a real tea bar gets a page
 * that says only what that tea bar said. Every guard sits OUTSIDE its tag, so
 * an empty value removes the ELEMENT and not merely its text: no eyebrow over
 * nothing, no heading over an empty stack, no white card holding a medallion
 * and no reason, no empty paragraph under a title.
 *
 * DERIVED, not authored:
 *   · THE NUMERAL. The design's demo data carries an `n` field ('01','02','03');
 *     our schema declares no numeral input, so it is computed from the DISPLAY
 *     index, zero-padded to two digits, and marked aria-hidden — ordinal
 *     decoration, and a screen reader already gets the order from the document.
 *     It and the medallion colour are the ONLY things keyed to the display
 *     index rather than the original one (R6): after a blank row is dropped the
 *     printed sequence must read 01-02-03, never 01-03, and the pastel cycle
 *     must not skip a hue. Everything an EDIT touches uses the ORIGINAL index,
 *     so deleting reason 2 can never misdirect a write into reason 3.
 *   · The medallion, its pastel wash and the card ground. Decoration; no
 *     data-field, nothing to announce.
 *
 * DELIBERATELY NOT RENDERED, so none of it reads as an oversight:
 *   · why.image and why.lead. Both are schema-declared and both are used by
 *     sibling templates, but this design's WHY-US has neither a plate nor a
 *     lead paragraph — it is eyebrow, headline, stacked cards. Adding either
 *     would be building a different section than the one handed over. No plate
 *     also means no .plate, no .cap, no role="img" and no alt anywhere in this
 *     file (R9): there is no upload here to give an accessible name to.
 *   · NO STAR ROW (R2). This section carries no review and no rating field, and
 *     the design draws no stars here. Stars belong to TESTIMONIALS and only
 *     ever drawn from a real numeric rating — five stars printed for a customer
 *     who gave no rating is a fabricated claim. A reason with no numeral does
 *     not get one invented either; the ordinal above is decoration, not data.
 *   · NO id ON THE SECTION. The page's ids are menu / about / gallery / visit /
 *     faq / main, and the design gives WHY-US none of them; the nav remaps a
 *     derived '#why' onto '#about'. An id here would create a target the
 *     navigation never points at and a second landing place for the same link.
 *   · NO .band-pink / .band-sage / .band-lilac. The wrapper offers all three
 *     and this section opts into none, as drawn: WHY-US sits on the page's own
 *     blush --paper with WHITE cards on it, and the three pastels appear only
 *     inside the medallions. Banding the section would put a pastel ground
 *     behind pastel medallions and flatten the one contrast it is drawn on.
 *   · NO onPage() ANCHOR HELPER (R7), and this is a decision rather than an
 *     omission. The design's WHY-US emits no href of any kind — no button, no
 *     link, no chip that navigates — so there is nothing to remap and a copied
 *     helper would ship as unreachable dead code in this one file, which is
 *     what a reviewer would flag instead. WhyBM, WhyBN and TrustBO each made
 *     the same call for the same reason. If a link is ever added here, copy the
 *     helper from a BO sibling with PAGE_ANCHORS = menu / about / gallery /
 *     visit / faq / main and ANCHOR_ALIAS mapping location,contact -> visit ·
 *     services,rooms -> menu · host,why -> about · work -> gallery ·
 *     book -> main, passing tel: / mailto: / http(s) through untouched.
 *   · NO PER-REASON ICON. A drawn pictogram claims WHAT the reason is about;
 *     the owner's words are the only signal this section may carry. The
 *     medallion holds a number, which claims nothing.
 *
 * DECISIONS a reader would otherwise take for oversights:
 *
 *   · SPECIFICITY: EVERY OVERRIDE OF A WRAPPER PRIMITIVE IS QUALIFIED BY ITS
 *     PARENT CLASS, and this is not decoration. Astro 5 scopes this sheet as
 *     `:where(.astro-HASH)` — VERIFIED by compiling the file and reading the
 *     emitted CSS, not assumed — and :where() contributes NOTHING to
 *     specificity. So a bare `.sip-why-t` is (0,1,0), while every PageBO
 *     primitive is `html[data-page="BO"] :where(…)` = (0,1,1) and WINS on the
 *     type selector. An earlier draft wrote .sip-why-kick, .sip-why-h2 and
 *     .sip-why-t unqualified and all three were silently dead: the eyebrow drew
 *     at the wrapper's .18em in --accent (the purple, not the design's deep
 *     purple), the headline kept `margin:0 0 .3em`, `line-height:1.12` and the
 *     22ch cap that leaves a CENTRED heading hugging the left of the wrap, and
 *     the reason's title drew at 700/1.12 instead of the design's 600/normal.
 *     `.sip-why-head …` and `.sip-why-card …` take each to (0,2,0), which
 *     outranks (0,1,1). AboutBO, GalleryBO and TrustBO all qualify for exactly
 *     this reason. Rules that override nothing the wrapper declares
 *     (.sip-why-head, .sip-why-list, .sip-why-card, .sip-why-body) are left
 *     unqualified on purpose — specificity bought without a fight is noise.
 *
 *   · THE h2 FONT-SIZE IS NOT RESTATED. The design draws this heading at
 *     clamp(30px,4vw,52px); the wrapper's shared .h2 primitive is
 *     clamp(28px,3.9vw,52px), and the wrapper owns a 760 pass that re-clamps
 *     it. NEITHER FLOOR EVER APPLIES: 3.9vw only falls below 28px under a 718px
 *     viewport and 4vw only falls below 30px under 750px, and at 760px and
 *     narrower the wrapper's own pass has already replaced the clamp outright.
 *     The real divergence is the SLOPE — 3.9vw against the design's 4vw — so
 *     between 761px and 1333px this heading renders 2.5% smaller than drawn:
 *     46.8px instead of 48px at a 1200px viewport, 50.7px instead of 52px at
 *     1300px, identical from 1333px up. Peak loss ~1.3px. The qualified
 *     selector below WOULD out-specify the 760 pass, so a local font-size would
 *     pin the design's clamp at every width and leave one section growing while
 *     fourteen siblings re-size; AboutBO and GalleryBO made the same call.
 *     Only what this section draws DIFFERENTLY is stated:
 *     line-height 1.08, margin .24em 0 0, and the released measure (the shared
 *     primitive caps at 22ch, which on a CENTRED heading renders as centred
 *     text inside a left-hugging 22ch box; the design gives this h2 no
 *     max-width at all, so the .wrap is its bound).
 *
 *   · THE TITLE'S LEADING IS `normal`, on purpose. The design's h3 carries no
 *     line-height and the design's own stylesheet sets none, so `normal` — with
 *     Baloo 2's own generous metrics — is literally what it draws. It is
 *     restated because PageBO's shared h1-h4 rule is 1.12, which is the h2's
 *     display leading and would set a 26px title far tighter than it was drawn
 *     the moment an owner's reason runs to two lines. Guessing a number would
 *     be a divergence of its own.
 *
 *   · THE CARD RADIUS IS THE DESIGN'S LITERAL 28px. R1 governs COLOUR; this is
 *     a length. --r-lg is 26px and --r-md is 18px, so no token holds 28px, and
 *     rounding to --r-lg would be a different drawing on the shape this whole
 *     section is made of. The MEDALLION instead uses var(--r-pill), not the
 *     design's `50%`: on a 76x76 box these are the same drawing, computed and
 *     not assumed — two 100px radii on one 76px side sum to 200 > 76, so CSS
 *     scales both by 76/200 = 0.38, giving 38px per corner, which is exactly
 *     half of 76, i.e. a full circle. Using the token keeps the medallion on
 *     the family's pill vocabulary.
 *
 *   · THE MEDALLION REUSES .fig, which already gives var(--disp) at 700 with
 *     tabular lining numerals — the design's figure exactly. Only the 32px and
 *     the COLOUR are local, and the colour MUST be local: .fig is --accent, and
 *     purple on any of these three pastels is precisely the failure PageBO's
 *     header warns about. .fig's line-height:1 is kept rather than the design's
 *     `normal`; the numeral is a single line centred in a fixed square box, so
 *     the two are the same drawing.
 *
 *   · THE PARAGRAPH DOES NOT REUSE .body. .body is clamp(14.5px,1.3vw,15.5px)
 *     / 1.72 / --ink-soft; the design's is a FLAT 15.5px / 1.78. Only the
 *     colour would have been inherited, and a section that overrides two of a
 *     primitive's three properties is not reusing it. Written locally from
 *     tokens only. font-family is left to inherit var(--sans) from body,
 *     exactly as it does in the design.
 *
 *   · THE CARD GAP IS `gap:14px` ON THE STACK, not the design's
 *     `margin-bottom:14px` on every card. Identical between cards; the
 *     difference is the 14px the design leaves BELOW the last one, which is an
 *     artefact of its repeat loop rather than a spacing decision — the space
 *     under this section belongs to GALLERY's own 80px.
 *
 *   · THE SECTION'S OWN PADDING IS NOT RESTATED. The design writes
 *     `padding:80px 28px 0`; the wrapper's shared
 *     `section { padding: clamp(48px,6.4vw,80px) 0 }` caps at exactly that 80px
 *     and keeps a fluid floor for a phone. The design's ZERO bottom is a
 *     WHOLE-PAGE rhythm — every unbanded section in that file pads top only —
 *     and belongs in the wrapper once, not re-derived in one section while
 *     fourteen siblings keep theirs. Flagged, not done here. The 28px gutter is
 *     likewise the wrapper's `.wrap` (min(1200px, 92vw)) for every section in
 *     this template; re-cutting it in this one file would inset these cards
 *     from the blocks above and below that they read as aligned with.
 *
 *   · `flex:none` FROM THE DESIGN'S MEDALLION IS DROPPED. Its parent is
 *     display:grid in the design too, so the property was already inert there;
 *     shipping it would be copying a no-op rather than a drawing.
 *
 * RESPONSIVE (R8). The wrapper owns the shared 760 and 520 TYPE pass; the grid
 * below is this section's own. There is no multi-column CONTENT grid here to
 * collapse — the cards are full-width and stacked at every width, exactly as
 * drawn — so the 900 and 520 passes instead tighten the one two-track
 * construct this section has: the decorative medallion rail beside the text.
 * THE LADDER IS MONOTONIC BY CONSTRUCTION: every FIXED length decreases at
 * each narrower step and none increases —
 *   rail track 88 -> 78 -> 66 · medallion 76 -> 68 -> 60 · numeral 32 -> 28 ->
 *   26 · card gap 26 -> 22 -> 18 · card padding 30/34 -> 26/26 -> 24/20 ·
 *   head margin 34 -> 30 -> 26.
 * The FLUID text track is the remainder and therefore gains room at each step,
 * which is the intent. There is not one clamp in this file, so there is no
 * floor in the 900 query that could outrank a cap in the 520 query. Nothing can
 * push the page sideways at 360px: both grids are minmax(0,…), the card and the
 * text column carry min-width:0, and the eyebrow, headline, title and
 * paragraph all carry overflow-wrap:anywhere. There is no button in this
 * section, so R8's white-space:normal pairing has nothing to apply to.
 *
 * FLAGGED, NOT FIXED HERE — the WRAPPER's own .h2 ladder inverts. PageBO's base
 * is clamp(28px,3.9vw,52px) and its 760 pass is clamp(26px,7vw,38px), so a
 * 761px viewport computes 3.9vw = 29.68px while a 760px viewport computes 7vw =
 * 53.2px capped to 38px: the headline GROWS by ~8.3px as the viewport narrows
 * past that breakpoint. It does so in all fifteen BO sections, not this one.
 * Restating font-size locally would fix it here and break the family's single
 * shared size curve, so it belongs in PageBO, once.
 *
 * TRACK COUNT vs ITEM COUNT: the stack takes any number of reasons. The design
 * fixes three (hint-placeholder-count="3") and gives each a hue; a fourth
 * reason restarts the pastel cycle at lilac rather than being refused or
 * squeezed.
 *
 * CONTRAST — COMPUTED from the hexes PageBO declares (sRGB relative luminance,
 * WCAG 2.x), not estimated, and rounded DOWN:
 *   --accent-deep on --lilac   7.39   (the eyebrow pill)
 *   --plum        on --pink-2  8.73   (medallion 2)
 *   --on-sage     on --sage    6.40   (medallion 3)
 *   --ink         on --card   16.85   (the reason's title)
 *   --ink-soft    on --card    7.54   (the reason's paragraph)
 * Nothing this section draws sits below AA. TWO CAVEATS, both the same one
 * PageBO makes for --muted: buildOverrideCss owns --card, --ink, --ink-soft and
 * --accent-deep and wins each with !important, so the first, fourth and fifth
 * figures are the NATIVE palette's and not a guarantee across every admin
 * scheme. --lilac, --pink-2, --sage, --plum and --on-sage are invisible to that
 * file, so those pairings hold whatever the scheme.
 *
 * CLASS PREFIX: `sip-why-` (Sipsip / why), matching the BO family's own `sip-`
 * prefix — `sip-about-`, `sip-gal-`, `sip-proof-` — for THIS template. Deliberately NOT the `tcw-`, `pcw-` or `why-*` sets of the WhyBM /
 * WhyBN / WhyBL siblings — an audit had to rename a whole block of classes that
 * had arrived verbatim from the template before them. Only the HOUSE STYLE is
 * inherited from those files (this doc block, the guard discipline, the
 * original-vs-display index rule); the palette, the stack, the medallion and
 * every metric are this design's.
 */
// `layout` is accepted because PageBO passes it to every section uniformly;
// this block reads nothing outside content.*.
interface Props { content: any; layout?: any; }
const { content } = Astro.props;

const why = content?.why || {};
const tag = typeof why.tag === 'string' ? why.tag.trim() : '';
// Nothing beyond trim() is done to the headline: it goes out through set:html
// so whatever markup the owner typed reaches the wrapper's colour-change em rule.
const headline = typeof why.headline === 'string' ? why.headline.trim() : '';

type Item = { title?: string; body?: string; desc?: string; description?: string };
const items: Item[] = Array.isArray(why.items) ? why.items : [];
const titleOf = (it: Item): string => String(it?.title ?? '').trim();
const bodyOf = (it: Item): string => String(it?.body ?? it?.desc ?? it?.description ?? '').trim();

// A reason the owner added but never filled would otherwise spend a whole white
// card, a pastel medallion and a numeral on nothing. Drop the blanks
// (whitespace counts as blank) but carry the ORIGINAL index `i` so every
// data-field still writes into the real array slot (R6).
const rows = items
  .map((it, i: number) => ({ i, title: titleOf(it), body: bodyOf(it) }))
  .filter((r) => Boolean(r.title || r.body));

// SECTION GATE (R5). Counts the CARDS only. lib/derive-content-defaults.ts emits
// why.tag ('Why us') and why.headline ('Why choose X') for every site while
// shipping items: [] — so a gate that counted the tag or the headline would be
// always-true and would ship an eyebrow and a headline over an empty stack on
// every first build.
const hasReasons = rows.length > 0;
---
{hasReasons && (
  <section class="sip-why">
    <div class="wrap">
      {(tag || headline) && (
        <div class="sip-why-head reveal">
          {tag && <span class="kick sip-why-kick" data-field="why.tag">{tag}</span>}
          {headline && <h2 class="h2 sip-why-h2" data-field="why.headline" set:html={headline}></h2>}
        </div>
      )}
      <div class="sip-why-list">
        {rows.map((r, d: number) => (
          /* `d` is the DISPLAY index and `r.i` is the ORIGINAL one. The numeral
             and the medallion hue are the only things keyed to `d`, so both the
             printed sequence and the pastel cycle stay unbroken after a blank
             row is dropped. The numeral is aria-hidden — the order is already
             carried by the document — and it carries no second literal
             aria-hidden anywhere (R9). The stagger tops out at the wrapper's
             last declared delay, which is 3 — so cards one to four each get
             their own step (none, .08s, .16s, .24s) and a FIFTH reason reveals
             together with the fourth. */
          <div class="sip-why-card reveal" data-delay={d > 0 ? String(Math.min(d, 3)) : undefined}>
            <span class="fig sip-why-n" aria-hidden="true">{String(d + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
            <div class="sip-why-body">
              {r.title && <h3 class="sip-why-t" data-field={`why.items.${r.i}.title`}>{r.title}</h3>}
              {r.body && <p class="sip-why-p" data-field={`why.items.${r.i}.body`}>{r.body}</p>}
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
)}
<style>
  /* Colour, type and metrics come only from PageBO's token vocabulary
     (--card --ink --ink-soft --lilac --pink-2 --sage --plum --accent-deep
     --on-sage --disp --r-pill, plus the .wrap, .kick, .h2 and .fig primitives).
     There is not one literal hex in this file (R1).

     (Never write a literal end-style-tag inside a comment in here — the parser
      would end the stylesheet on the spot and silently truncate the file.) */

  /* The section takes the wrapper's shared vertical padding, which caps at
     exactly the design's 80px; see the frontmatter for why the design's
     bottom-0 is a whole-page decision and is not restated here. */

  /* ── THE CENTRED HEAD. */
  .sip-why-head { text-align: center; margin-bottom: 34px; }

  /* The eyebrow is the design's LILAC PILL, built on the wrapper's .kick
     primitive so the family's tracked-caps eyebrow (face, 700, 11px, uppercase,
     inline-block, line-height 1.1) is inherited rather than re-declared.
     QUALIFIED BY .sip-why-head, and that is load-bearing: this sheet is scoped
     with :where(.astro-HASH), which adds no specificity, so a bare
     .sip-why-kick would be (0,1,0) and would LOSE to the wrapper's
     html[data-page="BO"] :where(.kick) at (0,1,1) — the tracking and the ink
     below would never land. With the parent it is (0,2,0) and wins.
     font-size is deliberately absent: BECAUSE the qualified selector now
     out-specifies :where(.kick), restating it would cancel the wrapper's 520
     pass. The tracking IS restated — the design draws .14em here, which is also
     the value that pass drops to, so it holds at every width. The ink is
     --accent-deep, the design's own, not .kick's --accent. */
  .sip-why-head .sip-why-kick {
    letter-spacing: .14em;
    color: var(--accent-deep);
    background-color: var(--lilac);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: var(--r-pill);
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  /* ── the headline. The wrapper's .h2 primitive carries the face, the clamp
        and --ink; only the three things this section draws differently are
        stated. Qualified by .sip-why-head for the same (0,2,0) vs (0,1,1)
        reason as the eyebrow — bare, none of the three would land, and the
        22ch cap in particular would leave this CENTRED heading hugging the
        left of the wrap with its text centred inside a narrow column. No
        font-size at any breakpoint in this file, so there is no clamp for a
        narrower viewport to invert (R8). */
  .sip-why-head .sip-why-h2 {
    line-height: 1.08;
    margin: .24em 0 0;
    max-width: none;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  /* ── THE STACK. Full-width cards at the design's 14px rhythm. `gap` rather
        than the design's per-card margin-bottom; see the frontmatter. */
  .sip-why-list {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 14px;
  }

  /* ── THE CARD. White, radius 28px, padded 30px 34px, drawn as a medallion
        rail beside the text and vertically centred — all the design's. The two
        custom properties are the medallion's pastel pairing; the base
        declaration is the design's FIRST hue, so a lone reason is lilac, and
        the two overrides carry the rest of the cycle. Position is the DISPLAY
        position on purpose (R6) — a dropped blank row must not leave a hole in
        the sequence. No token holds 28px, and this is a length, not a colour,
        so the design's number stands. */
  .sip-why-card {
    min-width: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 88px) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 26px;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 30px 34px;
    border-radius: 28px;
    background-color: var(--card);
    --sip-why-bg: var(--lilac);
    --sip-why-fg: var(--accent-deep);
  }
  .sip-why-card:nth-child(3n + 2) { --sip-why-bg: var(--pink-2); --sip-why-fg: var(--plum); }
  .sip-why-card:nth-child(3n + 3) { --sip-why-bg: var(--sage);   --sip-why-fg: var(--on-sage); }

  /* ── THE MEDALLION. .fig already gives var(--disp) at 700 with tabular lining
        numerals — the design's figure exactly. Only the size and the colour are
        local, and the colour MUST be local: .fig is --accent, and purple on any
        of these three pastels is the pairing PageBO forbids. Written as a
        descendant so it clears the wrapper's :where() primitive whatever the
        source order. 100px on a 76px box scales to 38px per corner — a full
        circle, which is the design's 50%. */
  .sip-why-card .sip-why-n {
    width: 76px;
    height: 76px;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    border-radius: var(--r-pill);
